# Cloudflare Pages response headers (static files only; /api/* Functions set their own).
#
# Long-term caching rests on one rule of this site: every reference to a .js, .css, font or model file carries ?v=N,
# and N is bumped whenever the file changes (tests/cache.test.mjs fails on an unversioned or mixed reference).
# The browser caches by full URL, so a bumped ?v= is fetched fresh and an unchanged one is never asked for again.
#
# Not listed here, on purpose: HTML pages, images, data/*.json, terrain tiles and model .json sidecars. They keep
# Pages' default (Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate + ETag): the browser asks every time and gets a 304.

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/models/*.glb
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
